WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.402
Russia's Vladimir Putin

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.770
rolling out the red carpet

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.170
for his,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.672
quote, dear friend

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.474
Chinese leader Xi Jinping

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.375
greeting each other

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.943
for their second day of meetings

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.344
in Moscow.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.413
Despite skepticism from the West

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.481
that the visit is more

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.348
about supporting

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.583
Russia and furthering

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:18.852
Beijing's own self-interests, Putin

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.854
and Xi signing an economic deal,

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.522
deepening their partnership,

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.857
and calling for an end

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.658
to actions that increase tensions

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.460
in the prolonged war in Ukraine.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.062
Many of you, in your mind,

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:29.629
of course,

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:30.530
we did not ignore

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.298
the situation around Ukraine.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:32.999
We believe that

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.768
many of the points on the peace plan

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:35.435
put forward by

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:36.803
China are consistent

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.071
with Russian approaches

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.706
and can be taken as the basis

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.041
of a peaceful settlement.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.176
When the West and Kiev are ready for it.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.744
But this readiness is

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.146
not observed on their side.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:47.881
Since the

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.782
war began,

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.716
Russia has become

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.951
far more dependent on China.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.253
China has been propping up

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.722
Russia's economy amid Western sanctions

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.690
by purchasing its energy,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.259
replacing Western suppliers

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.528
in electronics, cars and aircraft,

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.296
and providing an alternative

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.898
to the US dollar.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.566
That she is inviting Putin

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:07.801
to China this year

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:08.635
and told Putin

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.304
they share similar goals for noble goal.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.605
Putin says Russia

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.474
has closely studied Beijing's

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.342
peace proposal for Ukraine,

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:16.743
a plan

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.811
that Washington says

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:18.745
would solidify

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.847
Russia's grip on occupied land.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:25.785
China would not want to see Putin fail.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:28.655
It would set a terrible example

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.357
for the Chinese system.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:32.759
China and Russia

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.561
have a complicated history,

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.863
but their shared adversarial relationship

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.332
with Washington is driving them closer.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.934
This is a marriage of convenience,

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:41.768
not of affection.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.435
In Russia,

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.736
there's some cynicism

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.271
about Beijing's motives.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.340
On a Russian state TV talk show,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.209
this military pundit said

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:51.544
China can have only one ally,

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.079
China itself.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:55.782
China can only have one set of interests,

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.684
pro-Chinese ones.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.018
Chinese foreign policy

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.921
is utterly devoid of altruism, he wrote,

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.724
but Chinese state media is in overdrive,

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.559
touting the benefits of the Russia

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.961
China relationship.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.162
And it's all positive

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.697
comments on China's heavily

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.432
censored social media.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:15.301
This one says cooperation and win win.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.837
The next one says Long live China.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.139
Russia. Friendship.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.541
Disagreements, if any, are censored

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.676
by meeting with Putin.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:24.844
She wants to highlight

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.746
his role as a global statesman

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.448
that can offer an alternative

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:31.651
to the current world order.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.221
But Jake, the real tangible

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.256
outcome of this meeting

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.290
is Beijing

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.725
strengthening ties with Russia

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.760
in ways that benefits itself.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.061
These economic agreements

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.196
they've signed, it's likely

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.697
going to increase Russia's

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.466
reliance on China.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.467
Now, China's

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.935
policy is a bit contradictory,

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:51.171
but it really boils down to supporting

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:53.606
Putin while publicly declared neutrality,

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.775
but also paying no price.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:56.976
That's why the experts

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.678
I speak to say it's unlikely

00:02:58.678 --> 00:02:59.913
that China would provide

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.614
the kind of lethal aid to Russia

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.282
that would trigger

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.883
secondary sanctions Jake.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.051
All right, Selina Wang in Beijing,

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:05.685
thanks so much.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.719
Meanwhile,

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.689
Japan's prime minister Fumio Kishida

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.225
made a surprise trip to Ukraine,

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:13.159
where he met

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.160
with Ukraine's president

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.162
Volodymyr Zelensky and visited

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.430
Bhutia, the key

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.598
suburb synonymous

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.633
with Russia's atrocities

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.502
against the Ukrainian people.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:22.802
Because she

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:23.570
this trip

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.270
marks the first time

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:24.938
a Japanese prime

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.806
minister has visited an area

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.841
with ongoing fighting

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.276
since World War Two.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.177
CNN's Ivan

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.212
Watson is live for us

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.180
in the northeastern city of Kharkiv.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.115
And Ivan, the timing of this visit

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:39.752
seems pretty, pretty important.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:41.287
It does.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.555
And it does not seem like

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.923
it's it's a coincidence

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:44.757
that you had the leader

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.559
of China visiting Moscow.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.661
And then the same day

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.763
the Japanese prime minister visiting

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.733
Russia's enemy, the capital of Ukraine,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:57.103
Kishida Laying flowers in Buka, where

00:03:57.704 --> 00:04:01.040
there were discoveries of mass graves,

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.308
of people executed

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.010
with their hands tied behind their backs

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.178
after the Russian troops

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.012
withdrew

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.481
from that town on the outskirts of Kiev.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:12.352
Japan signaling its commitment to Ukraine

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:12.986
last month,

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:13.453
it pledged

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:16.089
some $5.5 billion in assistance

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:17.957
to the Ukrainian government

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.392
and has said that

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:22.095
it speaks out strongly against Russia's,

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:25.164
as it puts it, aggression in to Ukraine.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:26.332
In the meantime,

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:26.966
the Ukrainians

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.134
still watching this meeting

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:29.869
in Moscow closely.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:30.603
The Ukrainian

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.871
president, Volodymyr Zelensky.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.606
Zelensky has come out with statements

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:37.644
about the suggestion of a cease fire made

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:38.911
by Putin and Xi.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.179
Today, saying that

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.715
that nobody would be satisfied with that

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:43.950
right now,

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.652
going on to say that

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:47.754
that would simply freeze the conflict

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:48.721
and allow Russia

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.823
to regroup and attack again

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.191
sometime in the future.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.026
He says

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:55.762
Ukraine has its own peace formula

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.230
and that probably involves

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.598
Russian troops withdrawing

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.133
from Ukrainian territory

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.135
and he wants to share that directly

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.603
with the Chinese leader.

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.738
We don't know when these two leaders

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:06.639
will talk.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.507
And Ivan,

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:08.941
Ukraine and Russia are disputing

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:09.509
the details

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.777
of an attack in the Crimea

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:13.313
and town of John Coy.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.580
That's where a train

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.215
carrying Russian caliber

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.584
cruise missiles was destroyed.

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:19.652
What are Ukrainian officials

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:22.622
saying about this attack?

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:23.523
Right.

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.158
I mean, we have seen amateur video

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:26.759
of some huge explosion last night.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:29.028
The Ukrainians claim that they hit

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:31.197
a shipment of these caliber

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.432
cruise missiles.

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.666
We do not have independent

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:34.634
confirmation of that.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.935
The Russians say, hey,

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.804
our air defense has shot down

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:38.905
some kind of an attack.

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:40.239
Somebody was injured.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.574
They haven't said anything more

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:42.375
about whether or not

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:43.609
these missiles were hit.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:44.877
In the meantime, tonight,

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.045
within the last couple of hours,

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.513
we've heard about missile

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.082
strikes on the southern

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:51.484
Ukrainian port city of Odessa.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:52.185
The Ukrainian

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:53.853
say that they shot down

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.788
two of these cars,

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.223
59 missiles

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:59.792
that were launched by Russian warplanes.

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:02.362
But two more got through the air defenses

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.030
and have injured people.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.865
We're still waiting to find out more

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:08.067
about the extent of that damage.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:08.267
All right,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.902
Ivan Watson in Kiev, Ukraine for us.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:10.603
Thank you so much.

